AArch64 arm64-userword-handoff-fixed
(* Same protocol and same condition as arm64-userword-handoff-main; the only
   change is which field hands the slot over, and how.

   Under the fix, localCurrentEpoch is the ownership word and Release()
   unpublishes it with a release store (Volatile.Write), AFTER clearing
   threadId. That release store is ordered after every preceding memory
   operation of the departing thread -- including its EndInflightEnqueue write
   of the InflightInactive sentinel into its user word. The arriving owner's
   claim CAS reads-from that release store, so it acquires everything ordered
   before it.

   The user-word column was never part of the fix's design and is untouched by
   the diff, but the handoff it depends on is exactly the pairing the fix
   establishes. Upstream had no such pairing: the same message-passing shape
   with a plain handover store is architecturally open. *)
{ 0:X0=uw; 0:X1=tid; 0:X2=lce; 1:X0=lce; 1:X1=uw; uw=7; tid=3; lce=5; }
 P0            | P1               ;
 MOV X3,#9     | MOV X2,#0        ;
 STR X3,[X0]   | MOV X3,#1        ;
 STR XZR,[X1]  | CASAL X2,X3,[X0] ;
 STLR XZR,[X2] | LDR X4,[X1]      ;
exists (1:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=7)
